1
00:05:24,705 --> 00:05:30,705
The 'Maggie' is a comedy film directed by Alexander Mackendrick.

2
00:10:49,411 --> 00:10:55,411
The poor, elderly—and the wily, when it comes to parting those who can afford it from their money—Scottish skipper of a
broken-down old 'puffer' boat tricks an American tycoon into paying him to transport his personal cargo.

3
00:16:14,117 --> 00:16:20,117
When the tycoon learns of the trick, he attempts to track
down the boat and remove his possessions.

4
00:21:38,823 --> 00:21:44,823
Calvin B. Marshall, the American, played by Paul Douglas.

5
00:27:03,529 --> 00:27:09,529
Captain McTaggart, the Skipper, played by Alex Mackenzie.

6
00:32:28,235 --> 00:32:34,235
The Mate, played by James Copeland.

7
00:37:52,941 --> 00:37:58,941
The Engineer, played by Abe Barker.

8
00:43:17,647 --> 00:43:23,647
Doogie, the Wee Boy, played by Tommy Kearins.

9
00:48:42,352 --> 00:48:48,352
Pusey, played by Hubert Gregg.

10
00:54:07,058 --> 00:54:13,058
Hobson's Choice is a 1954 British romantic comedy film directed by David Lean.

11
00:59:31,764 --> 00:59:37,764
It is based on the 1916 play of the same name by Harold Brighouse.

12
01:04:56,470 --> 01:05:02,470
It stars Charles Laughton in the role of Victorian bootmaker Henry Hobson, John Mills as  timid but highly
talented employee Will Mossop, and Brenda de Banzie as Hobson's eldest, fiercely determined daughter.

13
01:10:21,176 --> 01:10:27,176
The film also features Prunella Scales in one of her first cinematic roles.

14
01:15:45,882 --> 01:15:51,882
Hobson's Choice won the British Academy Film Award for Best British Film 1954.

15
01:21:10,588 --> 01:21:16,588
The film explores themes of ship, scotland, glasgow, scotland, boat, skipper.

16
01:26:35,294 --> 01:26:41,294
The tone is lighthearted.
